{"sequence":29,"timestamp":"2026-03-30T11:10:55.615061569Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-2-21a3dd5d","body":"In e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes.rs, the doc comment for probe_successful_breeding (line 183) says \"Over 1 200 simulated hours (~50 days)\" but the implementation uses total_days = 60 (line 211), which is 1,440+ simulated hours. Update the doc comment to say \"Over 1 400 simulated hours (~60 days)\" to match the actual implementation.","dedup_key":"9f2644946733db80e97928888c271ce2a39d66a59592a879252e140d20e84160","run_id":"run-20260330093843","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":30,"timestamp":"2026-03-30T11:10:55.624242905Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-2-aa20fab2","body":"In the thermal_scenario_state fixture (e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes.rs ~line 427), the cool control arm finishes with condition 0.267, molt_stress 1.000, failed_molt_accum 1.000, and NO2 = 1.71 mg/L — a severely degraded state, not the healthy baseline the doc comment describes. Root cause: the AOB:NOB biomass ratio (2.0g:1.5g at equal Vmax 10.0) creates a structural nitrite bottleneck, and failed_molt_mortality_scale is not zeroed despite shrimp_base_mortality_per_day and shrimp_stress_mortality_scale being set to 0.0. The probe passes by accident (cool arm produces 8 juveniles before collapsing). Fix by either (a) increasing NOB biomass to >= AOB throughput (e.g., NOB 2.0g), (b) also zeroing shrimp_params.failed_molt_mortality_scale in the thermal fixture (as done in breeding_success_state at line 388), or (c) adding periodic water changes to control nitrite — any of which would make the cool arm a genuine healthy control and make the thermal comparison robust to retuning.","dedup_key":"e018efe9f07395501044b3875c77c6f2742eaf94c76c90d8134735e7711d28b7","run_id":"run-20260330093843","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":31,"timestamp":"2026-03-30T11:10:55.633416928Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-2-bdcd6707","body":"Thermal suppression never verifies the promised egg-dropping path. In `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:800-813`, `egg_dropping()` only fires on instability or temperature swings, not on a steady >30 C tank. The probe in `crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes.rs:532-608` just records `cool_egg_drops`/`warm_egg_drops` in the summary and never asserts them, so `all_shrimp_probes_summary` currently passes with both counts at zero. Either seed berried females / introduce the intended heat shock, or add a chronic-heat egg-drop mechanism, then assert the warm arm actually drops eggs.","dedup_key":"48cd0f52bb732adfef7b94b2858e7d7d1fe87a672076131446446c43f58aba65","run_id":"run-20260330093843","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":32,"timestamp":"2026-03-30T11:10:55.642635344Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-2-b317f92d","body":"The successful-breeding probe's \"two cycles\" check is weaker than the acceptance criterion. In `crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes.rs:211-257`, `berried_cycle_count` is incremented once per 10-day window if any berried female appeared; `crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes.rs:269-277` then treats `berried_cycle_count >= 2` as \"at least 2 complete reproductive cycles\". A single 14-day clutch can span two windows and satisfy this without two berried->hatch cycles. Track actual clutch/hatch transitions instead of window occupancy.","dedup_key":"57cce9024cbc961102173559e0bd6e4f105c3262f70f519f5e8e98aab3fff930","run_id":"run-20260330093843","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":33,"timestamp":"2026-03-30T11:10:55.651917881Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-2-d4d6dec5","body":"The thermal-suppression fixture is no longer isolating temperature, even though `crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes.rs:425-426` says it should. The setup in `crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes.rs:452-487` runs 60 days with no water changes and no chemistry envelope, and the assertions in `crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes.rs:544-583` only compare relative readiness/juvenile counts. On the current summary run the cool control finished at NO2=2.31 mg N/L, condition=0.066, and molt_stress=1.000, so the probe can pass while the control arm is in a nitrite crash. Add guardrails that keep the cool arm chemically stable or the test is confounded.","dedup_key":"0f6509325ef8877b178be212b8a6a3a178b9638a6b05a93443d5d854a11f4e4d","run_id":"run-20260330093843","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
